ROADMAP.md:48:## P0 – Windows Device Intake
ROADMAP.md:53:- [ ] **Strict report contract** — Validate `elistly.device-intake.v1`, enforce size/depth/type limits, and reject unsupported schemas before creating a preview.
ROADMAP.md:54:- [ ] **Side-effect-free preview** — Show exact create/update changes without mutating schema, dropdowns, entities, or persisted data.
ROADMAP.md:55:- [ ] **Explicit collision resolution** — Never silently merge people or computers when serial/hostname/email/account identifiers disagree.
ROADMAP.md:68:## P1 – Reliable import and export
ROADMAP.md:70:Selective JSON import/export exists; this milestone turns it into one compatible backup contract.
ROADMAP.md:72:- [ ] **Versioned backup envelope** — One schema-versioned full export that includes workspaces, settings, categories, types, entities, associations, and restorable metadata.
ROADMAP.md:76:- [ ] **CSV import** — Map columns to one entity type, preview validation, then bulk-create through the authoritative mutation path.
ROADMAP.md:77:- [ ] **Resource bounds** — Bound file size, rows, fields, nesting, and aggregate allocations before importing untrusted files.
ROADMAP.md:91:- [ ] **Mobile UX pass** — Test small screens, drawers, forms, modals, imports, and touch targets on real devices.
ROADMAP.md:108:- JSON import is partially implemented; it is no longer described as absent.
ROADMAP.md:112:- Windows Device Intake is now a first-class P0 requirement with its own contract and acceptance plan.
